# =============================================================================
# audit.rules — #442: Linux process-execution (execve) telemetry, the
# prerequisite for #441's 5 proc_creation_lnx_* Sigma rules.
#
# Install:
#   sudo cp audit.rules /etc/audit/rules.d/soc-execve.rules
#   sudo augenrules --load
#   sudo systemctl restart auditd   # only if augenrules --load didn't apply live
#
# REQUIRED companion setting in /etc/audit/auditd.conf:
#   log_format = ENRICHED
# Enriched format resolves auid/uid/gid inline as e.g. `auid=1000(alice)`
# instead of a bare `auid=1000` — configs/logstash.conf's auditd branch reads
# the parenthesized name when present, but degrades gracefully (falls back to
# the numeric id alone) if it isn't set, so this is a soft dependency: exec
# telemetry still flows without it, just without a resolved user.name. This
# repo has no separate UID->username lookup table (unlike
# configs/lookups/abac-attributes.csv, which is keyed on Windows account
# names already present in the source event), so ENRICHED is the only source
# for that field.
#
# Scope: only execve — this is process-execution telemetry, not a general
# file-integrity or syscall audit trail. Watches BOTH real users (auid>=1000,
# excluding the "unset" sentinel 4294967295 auid gets before a session has
# one — e.g. early boot/kernel-thread activity) and root-privileged execution
# (euid=0) regardless of auid, so a real-user session that escalates via sudo
# is still captured under its own auid, and the root branch also catches
# execution from system/service accounts (auid unset) running as root.
# arch=b64 and arch=b32 are both watched — a 32-bit binary on a 64-bit host
# enters the kernel through the b32 syscall table, and is invisible to a
# b64-only rule.
#
# NOT live-verified against a real auditd/kernel combination in this
# environment (no reachable Linux audit host) — confirm the exact field
# order/shape auditd emits on your kernel version before relying on
# configs/logstash.conf's grok patterns in production, same caveat this
# repo's other environment-blocked static-only changes carry (#454,
# tests/pipeline/test_mac_correlation.py's own docstring).

-D
-b 8192

-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=4294967295 -k soc_execve
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S execve -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=4294967295 -k soc_execve
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve -F euid=0 -k soc_execve_root
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S execve -F euid=0 -k soc_execve_root
